prompts.body:
Write a short email declining this request.

Request I received: {{request}}
Who it is from: {{sender:text|a colleague}}
Tone: {{tone:select(warm, formal, direct)|warm}}

Keep it under 120 words. Thank them, say no clearly in the first two sentences, give one honest reason, and offer one alternative.

Write three meta descriptions (max 155 characters each) for this page.

Page title: {{page_title}}
Main keyword: {{keyword}}
What the reader gets: {{benefit:text|a clear checklist they can use today}}

Use the keyword once, lead with the benefit, and end with a light call to action. Do not use clickbait.

Explain this metric change for a non-technical manager.

Metric: {{metric}}
Change: {{change}}
Context: {{context:long|No known releases or campaigns this week.}}

Give a two-sentence summary, three possible causes ranked by likelihood, and the first check for each. State what data you would need to be sure.

Write a one-page decision memo.

Decision to make: {{decision}}
Options: {{options:long}}
Constraints: {{constraints:text|Budget is fixed; decide by Friday.}}

Use the headings Context, Options, Recommendation, Risks and What would change my mind. Keep it under 350 words.

Turn my list into a plan for the week.

My list: {{tasks:long}}
Hours available per day: {{hours:number|6}}

Pick three priorities, put them in the best days, group small tasks into one block and leave one empty buffer slot per day. Show the plan as a table by day.

Rewrite my interview answer so it is clear and under 90 seconds spoken.

Question: {{question}}
My answer: {{answer:long}}

Use situation, action, result. Keep my facts; do not invent numbers. Then list two follow-up questions an interviewer might ask.

Draft a reply to this customer message.

Customer message: {{message:long}}
What we can offer: {{offer:text|a refund or a free replacement}}

Acknowledge the problem in the first sentence, avoid blame and jargon, state one concrete next step with a time, and keep it under 110 words.

Create a character sketch for a {{genre:text|mystery}} story.

Role in the story: {{role}}

Include their name, what they want, what stands in their way, a flaw, a secret, three specific habits, and one line of dialogue that shows their voice.

Create a text-to-image prompt for a product photo.

Product: {{product}}
Style: {{style:select(minimal studio, lifestyle, dramatic)|minimal studio}}

Specify the surface, background, lighting direction, lens and aspect ratio. Output one paragraph plus a short negative prompt.
